<!-- PAGE 20: FINAL REFLECTION -->
<h1 style="font-size: 18pt;">FINAL INTERNSHIP REFLECTION / SUMMARY</h1>
<p class="center italic" style="color: #475569;">A concise academic reflection (Recommended length 400–600 words)</p>

<h3>1. Work Completed</h3>
<p>During my 7-week internship (15 July to 02 September, 2026) at MAAN JEE Memorial Clinic, I developed an end-to-end Automated Ultrasound Examination Reporting and Clinical Management Web Application. The application was tailored to resolve the clinic's administrative and radiological workflow bottlenecks. Key modules delivered include a full-stack platform using Node.js, Express, TypeScript, and PostgreSQL; customized reporting templates for 6 core ultrasound exams (Whole Abdomen, Upper Abdomen, KUB, Pelvic, Obstetric, and Obstetric TVS); an Organ-Wise Findings Engine with one-click 'Set All Normal' presets; programmatic PDF generation with MAAN JEE Memorial Clinic letterhead formatting; digital QR code verification; and patient fee tracking.</p>

<h3>2. Technical & Professional Learning</h3>
<p>As a BS Software Engineering student, I strengthened my competencies across full-stack TypeScript development, relational PostgreSQL database design, RESTful API architecture, session-based authentication, and PDF buffer generation. Collaborating with clinical personnel at MAAN JEE Memorial Clinic also taught me how to translate real-world clinical requirements into intuitive software interfaces that eliminate user error under high daily patient loads.</p>

<h3>3. Challenges & Improvement</h3>
<p>A notable challenge was structuring patient ultrasound findings into organized organ categories without requiring doctors to re-type repetitive medical text. I solved this by building dynamic preset generators and a regex parsing engine that cleanly organizes notes under bold headings.</p>

<h3>4. Link to Academic Learning</h3>
<p>I directly applied academic concepts from Database Systems (normalization, transaction integrity, indexing), Web Engineering (client-server architecture, middleware, secure authentication), and Human-Computer Interaction (minimizing cognitive load for medical staff).</p>

<h3>5. Career Reflection</h3>
<p>Developing a real-world, clinical system for MAAN JEE Memorial Clinic demonstrated the tangible impact software engineering has on healthcare efficiency. This experience has solidified my career commitment to becoming a professional software engineer in healthtech and enterprise solutions.</p>

